Below you’ll find two complementary ways to get an **InputSource** for the external entity whose *system* URI is  

```text
http://astro.com/stylesheets/toptemplate
```

and whose *public* identifier is `"1234"` while you’re feeding the XML through a SAX‑filter chain.

---

## 1️⃣ Using the supplied helper (`SAXFilterFactoryImpl_resolveEntity`)  
If you already have access to the helper routine exposed as a “tool”, just invoke it once – no manual stream handling required.

| Step | Code |
|------|------|
| Call the helper | ```java<br>var inputSrc = functions.SAXFilterFactoryImpl_resolveEntity({<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;publicid: "1234",<br>&nbsp;&nbsp;sysId:   "http://astro.com/stylesheets/toptemplate"<br>});<br>// inputSrc now holds an InputSource instance (or null)<br>``` |

That’s all! The helper internally turns the matching system ID into a proper `URL`, opens the connection, wraps it in an `org.xml.sax.InputSource`, and hands it back to you. If the system ID isn’t one of the hard‑coded values inside the helper, it simply returns `null`, letting the parser fall back to its own resolution logic.

---

## 2️⃣ Writing your own `resolveEntity()` manually  
Sometimes you may prefer full control over the resolution process—e.g., logging, caching, or applying additional security checks. Below is a minimal but complete example showing how to do exactly that inside a custom SAX‑filter factory.

### 📌 Full Example

```java
import javax.xml.parsers.*;
import org.xml.sax.*;
import org.xml.sax.helpers.*;

import java.io.IOException;
import java.net.MalformedURLException;
import java.net.URL;

/**
 * A tiny SAX Filter Factory that demonstrates resolving an external entity.
 */
public class AstroStylesheetResolver extends DefaultHandler {

    /**
     * Override the EntityResolver interface so that the parser asks us first.
     *
     * @param publicId Public identifier of the entity (may be null).
     * @param systemId System identifier of the entity (must not be null).
     * @return An InputSource pointing at the stylesheet, or null to let the parser handle it.
     * @throws SAXException Any SAX exception thrown during processing.
     * @throws IOException  I/O error while opening the resource.
     */
    @Override
    public InputSource resolveEntity(String publicId, String systemId)
            throws SAXException, IOException {

        /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
        /* 1️⃣ Check whether this is the exact pair we care about              */
        /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
        if ("1234".equals(publicId) &&
                "http://astro.com/stylesheets/toptemplate".equals(systemId)) {

            /* -------------------------------------------------------------- */
            /* 2️⃣ Convert the system ID to a real URL                         */
            /* -------------------------------------------------------------- */
            URL url;
            try {
                url = new URL(systemId);
            } catch (MalformedURLException mue) {
                throw new SAXParseException(
                        "Invalid system ID format: " + systemId, null, mue);
            }

            /* -------------------------------------------------------------- */
            /* 3️⃣ Create an InputSource backed by the opened stream           */
            /* -------------------------------------------------------------- */
            InputSource source = new InputSource(url.openStream());

            /* Optional: set encoding explicitly if you know it               */
            source.setEncoding("UTF-8");

            /* Optionally record where we got the data from                    */
            source.setSystemId(url.toString());          // keeps original URI
            source.setPublicId(publicId);

            /* Return the ready-to-use InputSource                           */
            return source;
        }

        /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
        /* 4️⃣ Not the special case → ask the parser to continue normally      */
        /* ------------------------------------------------------------------ */
        return null;   // signals “use default” behaviour
    }

    /** Demo main that parses a file and uses the above resolver. */
    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        SAXParserFactory spf = SAXParserFactory.newInstance();
        SAXParser saxp = spf.newSAXParser();

        // Attach our handler/resolver
        ParserConfiguration config = new ParserConfiguration(); // placeholder
        // In practice you'd plug this into whatever framework you're using
        // For illustration:
        DocumentBuilderFactory dbf = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
        dbf.setNamespaceAware(true);
        dbf.setValidating(false);

        // Parse something that references the external entity...
        // saxp.parse(new File("myDocument.xml"), new AstroStylesheetResolver());
    }
}
```

#### What happens under the hood?

| Stage | Action |
|-------|--------|
| **Check IDs** | Only proceed if both identifiers match the expected strings. |
| **Create URL** | Turns the literal HTTP address into a `java.net.URL`. |
| **Open Stream** | Calls `url.openStream()`, giving you an `InputStream`. |
| **Wrap in InputSource** | Passes that stream to `new InputSource(stream)`; sets optional metadata like encoding, public/system IDs. |
| **Return** | Gives the parser a fully formed `InputSource`; returning `null` would defer to the default resolver. |

---

## 🎯 Quick Checklist

- [ ] Your XML processor actually calls `resolveEntity(...)` (most SAX parsers do automatically if you register an `EntityResolver`).  
- [ ] You’ve registered the resolver before starting the parse.  
- [ ] The system ID used in the XML matches exactly the string checked in your code.  
- [ ] Handle potential exceptions (`IOException`, `SAXException`) appropriately.  

With either approach you’ll end up handing the parser an `InputSource` that points straight at the remote stylesheet located at `http://astro.com/stylesheets/toptemplate`.

Happy parsing! 🚀

